  "term": "summative evaluation",
  "definition": "Summative evaluation is an end-point assessment used to judge how well a programme or scheme worked overall, based on participants’ experiences, satisfaction, and perceived outcomes. In this context, it looks back on the completed activity to decide its value and identify broad results and areas for improvement.",
